<title>USA: MBIA qualifies eight muni issues for bond insurance. [CORRECTED 15:50 GMT]</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies eight muni issues for bond insurance. [CORRECTED 15:50 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects by removing the incorrectly included Camanche Community School District, Iowa.)</p>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp. said on Wednesday that it qualified for insurance the following eight municipal bond issues scheduled for competitive sale today :</p>
<p>--Delaware, Del., $65 million General Obligations (GOs).</p>
<p>--Des Moines, Iowa, $21.68 million water revenues.</p>
<p>--Parke County Jail Building, Ind., $4.85 million first mortgage bonds.</p>
<p>--Lafourche School District, La., $10 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Holbrook, Mass., GOs $4.8 million.</p>
<p>--Geneva, N.Y., $1.18 million public improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Wilson School District, Pa., $34 million GOs, alternate bidding.</p>
<p>--Knoxville, Tenn., GOs, $23.34 million public improvement.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
